<title>UK: UK sees lower grain sales to Spain, eyes elsewhere.</title>
<headline>UK sees lower grain sales to Spain, eyes elsewhere.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK grain exports to top buyer Spain this 1996/97 season could fall to well below last season's 1.5 million tonnes if the Spanish crop is higher as forecast. British Cereal Exports, part of UK Home-Grown Cereals Authority, said exports to Italy and Portugal had been strong and would continue to be so.</p>
<p>Recent estimates put Spain's 1996 grains production at 19.7 million tonnes, almost double 1995's 10.8 million.</p>
<p>Almost 90 percent of UK grain exports of an estimated 4.5 million tonnes in 1995/96 have been to the European Union. -- London newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
</text>
